# python (scripts/build-portfolio-cover.py)
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Raw DataForSEO responses. They are machine-readable API dumps that nobody
# reads once the digested JSON and the markdown reports next to them exist, and
# they are what turned ordinary commits into hundreds of files and half a
# million lines — one commit on 12 October 2026 was 470,581 insertions, almost
# all of it these files. That volume is the most likely reason the Vercel–GitHub
# integration hit a secondary rate limit the same day and no deployment could
# start.
#
# They stay on disk, so every script's cache keeps working and a re-run costs
# nothing. The trade: a fresh clone has no cache, so running the measurements
# on another machine pays DataForSEO again. For a one-person project that is
# the cheaper side of the deal.
research/**/raw/
